I go back to that shop on Sunday morning.
There isn't a lot of crowd in the shop like yesterday.
That same Dada from yesterday is there.
I go to him and greet him.
"Dada, I bought this shirt from you yesterday," I tell him.
I take that new shirt out of the bag.
Along with it, I also give him yesterday's receipt.
Dada takes that shirt and the receipt in his hand.
"What is the problem, Madam?" he asks me.
I show him that shirt.
"This shirt is too small for me," I say.
"I want to exchange this shirt."
"Do you have a size bigger than this?"
Dada looks at the shirt's tag.
"Yes Madam, you will definitely get another shirt," he says politely.
"This shirt is a 'small' size."
"I will give you a shirt bigger than this."
"You wait one minute," saying this he goes towards the cupboard.
I stand right there and wait for him.
